#N Wireworld loop
#C A ring of conductor carrying one electron, which circulates for ever
#C with a period of twelve. The corners are chamfered on purpose: a square
#C corner gives its cell three wire neighbours, and the head then ignites
#C two of them and the electron splits.
#C Constructed for this library, not transcribed from anywhere.
x = 6, y = 4, rule = Wireworld
